      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "[Only write solution when there is no clear-cut or unique solution.]\nWe can use the logarithm to determine the first digit of a number in a given base.\n\nLet's start by finding the logarithm base $8$ of $473$. This will give us the power to which $8$ must be raised to get $473$. Since $473$ is between $256$ and $4096$ (the range for base $8$ from $1$ to $7$), we can conclude that the logarithm base $8$ of $473$ is between $2$ and $3$. Specifically, it is closer to $2$.\n\nTherefore, the first digit in base $8$ is $\\boxed{1}$.\n\nThis method works for any positive integer value, and can be generalized to larger numbers or in any number of digits.",
