    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the first digit of the base $8$ representation of $473_{10}$, we can use the properties of logarithms to count the number of digits in base $8$.\n\nWe want to find the digit before the decimal point. We can calculate it using the base conversion formula:\n\n$$ 473_{10} = d_{n-1} b^{n-1} + d_{n-2} b^{n-2} + \\dots + d_{1} b^1 + d_{0} b^0 $$\n\nIn the above equation, each $d_i$ is either $0$ or $1$, indicating whether the digit $i$ is significant or not. To find the first significant digit, we need to find the largest power of $8$ that is less than or equal to $473$.\n\n$$ 8^3 = 512 \\quad (> 473) $$\n$$ 8^2 = 64 \\quad (< 473 $$\n\nSince $8^2$ is less than $473$, the first significant digit of $473_{10}$ is the digit before $8^2$.\n\nTherefore, the first digit of the base $8$ representation of $473_{10}$ is $1$.\n\n\\boxed{1}",
