      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine the first digit of the base $8$ representation of $473_{10}$, we first convert $473_{10}$ to a base $8$ number using long division.\n\nThe procedure for long division can also be described using the arithmetic operators. Let's use them, and take the following steps:\n\n\\begin{align*}\n\\begin{array}{c|cccc}\n\\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & 2 & 9 & 7 \\\\\n\\cline{2-5}\n8 & 4 & 7 & 3 \\\\\n\\multicolumn{2}{r}{2} & 2 & 4 & -2 & 1\\\\\n\\cline{2-5}\n\\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & 4 & 9 & 3 & 0 \\\\\n\\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & 4 & 8 & 0 & -4 & 7\\\\\n\\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & 0 & 1 & 3 & -0 & 6\\\\\n\\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & 0 & 0 & 7 & 3 & -0 & 3\\\\\n\\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 0 -0 & 3 & -1 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\end{align*}\n\nThus, $473_{10}=2\\cdot8^3+9\\cdot8^2+7\\cdot8^1+0\\cdot8^0$.\n\nTherefore, the first digit is $2$.\n\nSo, $\\boxed{2}$ is the answer.",
